================================================================================
bitnet.cpp public API mirror — legal attribution
================================================================================

This crate is a CLEAN-ROOM RUST RE-IMPLEMENTATION of the kernel-task
layer of microsoft/BitNet (`bitnet.cpp`).

The following identifiers are mirrored from upstream:

  - Free functions: ggml_bitnet_init, ggml_bitnet_can_mul_mat,
                    ggml_bitnet_mul_mat_task_compute,
                    ggml_bitnet_transform_tensor,
                    ggml_bitnet_get_type_traits
  - Tensor type tag: GGML_TYPE_I2_S = 40
  - Data layout: i2_s 2-bit signed weight encoding (00 → 0, 01 → +1,
                 10/11 → -1), 4 weights per byte little-endian
  - Block layout: q8_0 (1 × f16 scale + 32 × i8)

No upstream source code has been copied. The API names are used under
the rule of Google v. Oracle America, 593 U.S. ___ (2021) (API fair
use), the same legal posture as the kami-engine nv-compat layer per
ADR-2605261800 §D11.

